WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.708 --> 00:00:32.583
<b>Here, Lord Krishna explains</b>

2
00:00:32.583 --> 00:00:39.041
<b>that One who attains peace</b>
<b>of mind is freed from all sorrows.</b>

3
00:00:39.041 --> 00:00:44.291
<b>Such a person, with a joyful heart,</b>
<b>gains unwavering wisdom.</b>

4
00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:52.708
<b>In the previous verse, we learned</b>

5
00:00:52.708 --> 00:00:56.250
<b>that when one lives a </b>
<b>disciplined and regulated life,</b>

6
00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:59.000
<b>their mind attains peace</b>

7
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.083
<b>and becomes pure.</b>

8
00:01:01.083 --> 00:01:08.458
<b>This means the mind has freed </b>
<b>itself from harmful attachments.</b>

9
00:01:08.458 --> 00:01:10.083
<b>For instance</b>

10
00:01:10.083 --> 00:01:15.500
<b>once someone gives up </b>
<b>sweets or sugar for their health</b>

11
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.166
<b>and adopts a balanced diet,</b>

12
00:01:18.166 --> 00:01:20.541
<b>making it a consistent practice,</b>

13
00:01:20.541 --> 00:01:26.333
<b>the mind's craving for</b>
<b>sweets gradually disappears.</b>

14
00:01:26.333 --> 00:01:28.791
<b>The mind has now found peace,</b>

15
00:01:28.791 --> 00:01:31.083
<b>distancing itself from that particular desire.</b>

16
00:01:31.083 --> 00:01:37.000
<b>And isn't the removal of any such </b>
<b>desire indeed the purification of mind?</b>

17
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:40.791
<b>When the mind thus</b>
<b>distances itself from all cravings</b>

18
00:01:40.791 --> 00:01:43.333
<b>and becomes pure and peaceful,</b>

19
00:01:43.333 --> 00:01:46.708
<b>three significant transformations occur in life,</b>

20
00:01:46.708 --> 00:01:50.125
<b>which this verse describes:</b>

21
00:01:50.125 --> 00:01:51.916
<b>First transformation</b>

22
00:01:51.916 --> 00:01:55.250
<b>All sorrows of such a person cease to exist.</b>

23
00:01:55.250 --> 00:02:01.625
<b>This doesn't mean that life's struggles </b>
<b>and challenges disappear completely.</b>

24
00:02:01.625 --> 00:02:05.958
<b>Struggles and challenges are integral parts of life.</b>

25
00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:08.541
<b>Here, the cessation of sorrow means</b>

26
00:02:08.541 --> 00:02:13.083
<b>that since the person has gained </b>
<b>control over their senses</b>

27
00:02:13.083 --> 00:02:15.583
<b>and renounced attachments,</b>

28
00:02:15.583 --> 00:02:22.416
<b>they no longer expect specific </b>
<b>outcomes from life's events.</b>

29
00:02:22.416 --> 00:02:25.916
<b>For them, no outcome is good or bad, </b>

30
00:02:25.916 --> 00:02:28.875
<b>no event is favorable or unfavorable.</b>

31
00:02:28.875 --> 00:02:35.625
<b>So when nothing is perceived as adverse, where </b>
<b>can sorrow exist? It's simply vanished, hasn't it?</b>

32
00:02:35.625 --> 00:02:37.583
<b>Second transformation</b>

33
00:02:37.583 --> 00:02:40.500
<b>Because sorrows have ceased,</b>

34
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:44.750
<b>the person becomes joyful-hearted.</b>

35
00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:46.750
<b>Third transformation</b>

36
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:51.666
<b>A person with a joyful heart </b>
<b>develops steady wisdom.</b>

37
00:02:51.666 --> 00:02:58.041
<b>Such a person with steady wisdom </b>
<b>views life with great clarity and peace,</b>

38
00:02:58.041 --> 00:03:03.625
<b>living through well-reasoned decisions.</b>

39
00:03:08.416 --> 00:03:12.166
<b>Why do we experience suffering in life?</b>

40
00:03:12.166 --> 00:03:17.291
<b>Why do we experience negativity towards life?</b>

41
00:03:17.291 --> 00:03:19.708
<b>Perhaps you'll say that</b>

42
00:03:19.708 --> 00:03:25.125
<b>life's events are the cause of both.</b>

43
00:03:25.125 --> 00:03:29.375
<b>But is that really true?</b>

44
00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:34.958
<b>Are events really the cause?</b>

45
00:03:34.958 --> 00:03:36.708
<b>Rain pours down</b>

46
00:03:36.708 --> 00:03:39.166
<b>your clothes get wet,</b>

47
00:03:39.166 --> 00:03:41.416
<b>and you become distressed.</b>

48
00:03:41.416 --> 00:03:42.500
<b>Yet</b>

49
00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:50.375
<b>there's someone else who deliberately enjoys </b>
<b>that same rain,letting themselves get drenched.</b>

50
00:03:50.375 --> 00:03:55.875
<b>Was the rain itself the cause of distress or joy?</b>

51
00:03:55.875 --> 00:03:57.333
<b>Here's another example:</b>

52
00:03:57.333 --> 00:04:03.791
<b>A colleague points out an error in your plan.</b>

53
00:04:03.791 --> 00:04:10.333
<b>You feel grateful that the mistake was </b>
<b>caught before implementation</b>

54
00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:13.291
<b>and you can fix it.</b>

55
00:04:13.291 --> 00:04:17.750
<b>Yet another person might become </b>
<b>angry at this same situation,</b>

56
00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.958
<b>refusing to acknowledge the mistake.</b>

57
00:04:20.958 --> 00:04:26.375
<b>The same event, yet two completely </b>
<b>different experiences,</b>

58
00:04:26.375 --> 00:04:29.125
<b>two opposite reactions.</b>

59
00:04:29.125 --> 00:04:31.416
<b>The difference lies not in the events,</b>

60
00:04:31.416 --> 00:04:36.708
<b>but in the state of mind, in perspective.</b>

61
00:04:36.708 --> 00:04:46.541
<b>What happens is less important</b>
<b>than how you receive it.</b>

62
00:04:46.541 --> 00:04:53.041
<b>And this determines the difference</b>
<b>between joy and sorrow.</b>

63
00:04:53.041 --> 00:04:56.458
<b>If your mind is completely at peace,</b>

64
00:04:56.458 --> 00:05:01.708
<b>would you view any event negatively? </b>

65
00:05:01.708 --> 00:05:02.916
<b>Of course not.</b>

66
00:05:02.916 --> 00:05:10.041
<b>And if negativity disappears, can sorrow persist?</b>

67
00:05:10.041 --> 00:05:11.958
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

68
00:05:11.958 --> 00:05:16.083
<b>This doesn't mean all pain will vanish.</b>

69
00:05:16.083 --> 00:05:16.916
<b>But</b>

70
00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:20.958
<b>you'll see pain objectively.</b>

71
00:05:20.958 --> 00:05:26.458
<b>You won't amplify it with negativity.</b>

72
00:05:26.458 --> 00:05:34.250
<b>You'll also understand that this pain exists </b>
<b>today but will pass tomorrow.</b>

73
00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:41.833
<b>Isn't viewing life with such gentleness the</b>
<b>end of unnecessary suffering?</b>

74
00:05:46.625 --> 00:05:51.708
<b>Everyone wishes for </b>
<b>their family's lasting happiness.</b>

75
00:05:51.708 --> 00:05:55.041
<b>It's why they work so hard.</b>

76
00:05:55.041 --> 00:06:02.041
<b>Hard work to earn, providing comforts, </b>
<b>planning vacation trips,</b>

77
00:06:02.041 --> 00:06:04.791
<b>and many such efforts.</b>

78
00:06:04.791 --> 00:06:07.333
<b>The goal is singular</b>

79
00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:09.041
<b>family happiness.</b>

80
00:06:09.041 --> 00:06:12.541
<b>These all have their importance,</b>

81
00:06:12.541 --> 00:06:19.458
<b>but won't these needs for happiness </b>
<b>keep growing with time?</b>

82
00:06:19.458 --> 00:06:24.583
<b>Is this the right path to finding joy?</b>

83
00:06:24.583 --> 00:06:29.541
<b>Will such happiness endure?</b>

84
00:06:29.541 --> 00:06:35.541
<b>So how can we keep our family </b>
<b>content for the long term?</b>

85
00:06:35.541 --> 00:06:43.541
<b>Establishing some discipline and rules in </b>
<b>life can certainly be one way.</b>

86
00:06:43.541 --> 00:06:47.541
<b>Yes, this might seem paradoxical,</b>

87
00:06:47.541 --> 00:06:48.750
<b>but</b>

88
00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:51.083
<b>consider this</b>

89
00:06:51.083 --> 00:06:55.041
<b>who enjoys a sweet treat more,</b>

90
00:06:55.041 --> 00:06:58.541
<b>who appreciates its taste better</b>

91
00:06:58.541 --> 00:07:01.833
<b>one who indulges occasionally?</b>

92
00:07:01.833 --> 00:07:05.625
<b>Or one who's become habituated to it?</b>

93
00:07:05.625 --> 00:07:09.666
<b>And which approach is better?</b>

94
00:07:09.666 --> 00:07:12.333
<b>If life remains unregulated,</b>

95
00:07:12.333 --> 00:07:18.000
<b>and happiness depends solely</b>
<b>on comforts and means,</b>

96
00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:23.625
<b>the mind quickly grows indifferent to </b>
<b>one comfort and demands another,</b>

97
00:07:23.625 --> 00:07:27.708
<b>abandons one source of </b>
<b>pleasure to chase another,</b>

98
00:07:27.708 --> 00:07:32.083
<b>discards one entertainment to pursue the next.</b>

99
00:07:32.083 --> 00:07:34.166
<b>However,</b>

100
00:07:34.166 --> 00:07:38.708
<b>when means and comforts are regulated,</b>

101
00:07:38.708 --> 00:07:41.583
<b>the mind understands their value,</b>

102
00:07:41.583 --> 00:07:44.958
<b>remains content with them longer.</b>

103
00:07:44.958 --> 00:07:51.708
<b>Gradually, it becomes less dependent </b>
<b>on them for happiness.</b>

104
00:07:51.708 --> 00:07:54.875
<b>A regulated life is a happy life.</b>

105
00:07:54.875 --> 00:07:56.500
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

106
00:08:01.166 --> 00:08:02.958
<b>In professional life,</b>

107
00:08:02.958 --> 00:08:06.208
<b>what kind of people are more active?</b>

108
00:08:06.208 --> 00:08:07.541
<b>More</b>

109
00:08:07.541 --> 00:08:09.500
<b>efficient?</b>

110
00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:11.833
<b>Those who remain happy,</b>

111
00:08:11.833 --> 00:08:12.791
<b>or</b>

112
00:08:12.791 --> 00:08:16.208
<b>those who stay constantly worried?</b>

113
00:08:16.208 --> 00:08:22.083
<b>Happiness has a direct connection </b>
<b>to human efficiency.</b>

114
00:08:22.083 --> 00:08:27.750
<b>Here, happiness doesn't mean </b>
<b>being overly excited always.</b>

115
00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:32.916
<b>It means an inner contentment </b>
<b>and sense of security,</b>

116
00:08:32.916 --> 00:08:33.541
<b>and</b>

117
00:08:33.541 --> 00:08:38.375
<b>feeling grateful in every situation.</b>

118
00:08:38.375 --> 00:08:41.458
<b>Such a person thinks positively,</b>

119
00:08:41.458 --> 00:08:43.125
<b>and this</b>

120
00:08:43.125 --> 00:08:50.541
<b>motivates them to seek solutions rather </b>
<b>than worry about problems,</b>

121
00:08:50.541 --> 00:08:53.416
<b>enhancing their efficiency.</b>

122
00:08:53.416 --> 00:08:56.916
<b>If you hold a leadership </b>
<b>position in an organization,</b>

123
00:08:56.916 --> 00:09:02.166
<b>strive to develop such thinking </b>
<b>among your colleagues.</b>

124
00:09:02.166 --> 00:09:06.125
<b>And if you're an individual worker,</b>

125
00:09:06.125 --> 00:09:09.500
<b>find contentment within,</b>

126
00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:12.375
<b>remain grateful in every situation.</b>

127
00:09:12.375 --> 00:09:17.541
<b>Inner satisfaction and gratitude will</b>
<b>not only keep you happy</b>

128
00:09:17.541 --> 00:09:18.291
<b>but</b>

129
00:09:18.291 --> 00:09:21.666
<b>also increase your efficiency.</b>

130
00:09:21.666 --> 00:09:27.916
<b>And this Gita's purpose is to </b>
<b>awaken this feeling within you.</b>

131
00:09:27.916 --> 00:09:31.375
<b>Many paths have opened before you,</b>

132
00:09:31.375 --> 00:09:35.833
<b>many more remain to unfold.</b>

133
00:09:35.833 --> 00:09:37.791
<b>Just keep walking along.</b>

